 "intro": {
  "title": "THRESHOLD BEACH",
  "lines": [
   "The Gate set you down at the edge of the last water on the world.",
   "The people who came before you are standing on the sand."
  ]
 },
 "outro": "Next: the Glass Steppe. East of the cliff the sea bed runs to the horizon, and there is a causeway across it.",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "start",
   "at": [11, 28],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "SIGNAL HOUSE",
   "text": "Calder, you are through. I have you for as long as the Gate holds behind you. After that it is just the set and the dark."
  },
  {
   "id": "seal",
   "at": [16, 28],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Door is shut. Signal House, no answer. Logging it anyway: day one, a beach, the Gate dark behind me."
  },
  {
   "id": "rows",
   "at": [21, 28],
   "radius": 5,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Oilskins. Marrow boat crews in two rows, facing the water. They were put here and told to wait."
  },
  {
   "id": "bell",
   "at": [26, 28],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "A bell, a long way off across the lake, struck slowly. Nine strokes, then nothing. The fog-bell on the north pier at home does that, on the ninth stroke of the tide table."
  },
  {
   "id": "camp",
   "at": [21, 19],
   "radius": 2.5,
   "speaker": "CAMP LEDGER",
   "text": "WATER: the lake is salt. FOOD: nine days. Two of ours went out in the night and stood on the sand. Keep moving. Keep the lamp lit."
  },
  {
   "id": "north",
   "at": [31, 19],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "Singers on the north dune. Their rounds shake your aim. Rock to rock, and do not stand in the open."
  },
  {
   "id": "breach",
   "at": [46, 28],
   "radius": 2.5,
   "speaker": "MARROW GIRL LOG",
   "text": "Third night of the Hush. Skipper took her out past the bar to get clear. The sea opened under the keel. We did not sink. We arrived."
  },
  {
   "id": "engine",
   "at": [62, 27],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Iron plate, a boiler gone cold, and the stair to the deck is up the north end. The wood is Marrow oak. I know the smell."
  },
  {
   "id": "deck",
   "at": [66, 11],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "From the deck you can see the whole cove. And the only other thing standing up out here: needles, three of them, a long way off."
  },
  {
   "id": "winch",
   "at": [60, 10],
   "radius": 2.5,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "A winch lever on the wheelhouse wall. It works the gate at the east end of the deck: nothing else here is that well kept."
  },
  {
   "id": "cleft",
   "at": [78, 28],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "A cut in the cliff, and wind coming through it. First moving air I have felt on this world."
  },
  {
   "id": "hollow",
   "at": [21, 40],
   "radius": 2,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The back wall of this hut rings hollow."
  }
 ],
